pysisyphus 1.0.0: 0006-eulerpc-mass-weighted-step-length

What: EulerPC measures the integration (step) length in mass-weighted coordinates, bohr·amu½; pysisyphus 1.0.0 converts it back to plain Cartesian bohr.
Test: Measured mass-weighted steps on every EulerPC run: median 0.1000 (0.10 runs) and 0.0500 (0.05 runs) bohr·amu½; with the 1.0.0 length a 'step' of 0.10 gave 0.35 bohr·amu½ (attempt1_step_in_plain_bohr).

--- a/pysisyphus/irc/EulerPC.py
+++ b/pysisyphus/irc/EulerPC.py
@@ -92,9 +92,9 @@
 
     def get_integration_length_func(self, init_mw_coords):
         def get_integration_length(cur_mw_coords):
-            """Returns length of integration path done in mass-weighted coordinates
-            in un-mass-weighted coordinates."""
-            return np.linalg.norm((cur_mw_coords - init_mw_coords) / self.m_sqrt)
+            """Returns length of integration path in mass-weighted coordinates
+            (bohr·amu½)."""
+            return np.linalg.norm(cur_mw_coords - init_mw_coords)
 
         return get_integration_length
 
